  "worked_solution": "Let $p$ represent the daily profit in this game. There are $10,000$ possible numbers that can be selected. One of these numbers is the winning number. In the game, there are two possible outcomes:\n\n- If the player's number is selected, they win $$2,000.$ This means the player\u2019s profit is $$2,000-$2=$1,998,$ so we have $p=1998.$\n\n- If the player's number is not selected, they lose $$2,$ so we have $p=-2.$\n\nThe probabilities for the outcomes are\n\n$$\nP(1998)=\\frac{1}{10,000},\\,P(-2)=1-\\frac{1}{10,000}=\\frac{9,999}{10,000}.\n$$\n\nLet's summarize this in a table. If $p$ is the profit (in dollars) on a single game, and $f(p)$ is the probability mass function for $p,$ then we have the following:\n\n| $p$ | $1998$ | $-2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(p)$ | $\\frac{1}{10,000}$ | $\\frac{9,999}{10,000}$ |\n\nTherefore, the expected value of $p$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[p] & =1998\\cdot f(1998)+(-2)\\cdot f(-2) \\\\  & =1998(\\frac{1}{10,000})-2(\\frac{9,999}{10,000}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1998}{10,000}-\\frac{19,998}{10,000} \\\\  & =-\\frac{18,000}{10,000} \\\\  & =-1.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expected profit is $-$\\,1.8.$",
